// Config for the two Fly demo apps, baked into the image at
// /etc/docket.kdl (fly.toml points DOCKET_CONFIG at it). Binds wide
// because Fly's edge routes to the machine, not to localhost. What makes
// them demos is the `dev` feature fly.toml builds with: fixture data
// instead of JMAP, and a stand-in identity in place of the identity
// headers that Caddy (caddy-tailscale) supplies in front of the real
// deployment. The database sits on the machine's own disk, which a deploy
// replaces, so each deploy starts from the fixtures again.
bind "0.0.0.0:3000"
database "/tmp/docket.db"
log info
